			"type": "text",
			"text": "Iberobatrachus is a frog discovered in Spain dating back to the Early Cretaceous. Its name is a mix of 'Ibero' a reference to the iberian peninsula, the peninsula that spain and portugal is in, and 'batrachus' meaning frog. It was a rather small animal, being around 4 centimeters. We have two nearly complete fossils of these animals, giving us a good idea of what they looked like."
